 fix this error, switch to a Node.js or pnpm version the package accepts, or turn `engineStrict` off for an `engines.node` mismatch."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/docs/package_json.md","lines":["@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ the install fails."," With [`engineStrict`](./settings/cli.md#enginestrict) enabled, an incompatible"," `engines.node` in the project or in a dependency fails the install. Optional"," dependencies are exempt. With it disabled, an incompatible `engines.node` in","-the project prints a warning.","+the project or a required dependency prints a warning."," "," In a workspace, these checks apply to every workspace project. A project whose"," `os`, `cpu`, or `libc` excludes the current platform prints a warning."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/docs/settings/cli.md","lines":["@@ -70,8 +70,8 @@ directory."," "," If this is enabled, installation fails when the project or a dependency"," declares an `engines.node` range that does not accept the current Node.js","-version. When it is disabled, an incompatible project prints a warning and the","-install continues.","+version. When it is disabled, an incompatible project or required dependency","+prints a warning and the install continues."," "," Regardless of this setting, installation fails if the project's `engines.pnpm`"," does not accept the running pnpm version."],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm11/cli/default-reporter/src/logStreams.ts","lines":["@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ import type { StreamParser } from '@pnpm/logger'"," import * as Rx from 'rxjs'"," import { filter } from 'rxjs/operators'"," ","+import type { InstallCheckEvent } from './reporterForClient/reportInstallChecks.js'"," import type { ReporterPnpmConfig } from './ReporterPnpmConfig.js'"," "," interface LogsByStream {","@@ -11,7 +12,7 @@ interface LogsByStream {","   fetchingProgress: logs.FetchingProgressLog","   executionTime: logs.ExecutionTimeLog","   hook: logs.